ARTICLE 3 — INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY AND PATENT RIGHTS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

3.1  OWNERSHIP: All intellectual property rights in and to the Software,
     including all copyrights, patents, trade secrets, and trademarks, are
     and shall remain the exclusive property of Mehmet Zumrut. This License
     does not convey any ownership interest.

3.2  PATENT PENDING NOTICE: The following technical innovations embodied in
     the Software are covered by one or more pending patent applications:

       (a) Multi-layer deception firewall architecture combining XDP BPF at
           NIC driver level, TC eBPF traffic control, nftables decoy network,
           and LSM audit in a unified, cryptographically signed orchestration
           pipeline;

       (b) Passive eBPF observation architecture providing zero-write,
           zero-block kernel-level monitoring via ring buffer event delivery,
           enforced at BPF verifier level;

       (c) Kernel-level RBAC enforcement via user namespace UID range
           cryptographic isolation preventing cross-department privilege
           escalation at the kernel scheduler level;

       (d) Ed25519-signed command bus architecture for immutable orchestrator
           state management with append-only forensic audit trail;

       (e) Real-time behavioral TTP correlation engine mapping kernel
           tracepoint event sequences to MITRE ATT&CK identifiers with
           zero disk I/O requirement.

3.3  PATENT MARKING: Products or services incorporating this Software must
     include appropriate patent marking referencing the applicable patent
     numbers once issued, per 35 U.S.C. § 287.

3.4  NO PATENT LICENSE: This License does not grant any license under any
     patent, patent application, or patent right of the Licensor, except as
     strictly necessary to exercise the limited rights granted in Article 1.
     Any act that would constitute infringement of any patent held or applied
     for by the Licensor requires a separate Patent License Agreement.

